 "verdict": {
  "max_age_guard": "STOP",
  "reasoning": [
   "no threshold shows a detectable benefit over unguarded at this resolution: maxage24 -3.84 CI[-11.88,+3.53], maxage48 -3.34 CI[-9.81,+3.00], maxage96 -1.28 CI[-6.66,+2.88]. With n=32 the design resolves ~7-16 per contrast (see power.mde_vs_unguarded_lancer), at or above the +5 advancement threshold for most contrasts, so stop means no detectable benefit, not a proven zero effect.",
   "monotone in how hard the guard binds: the more it overrides the scorer the worse the return (-3.84 at A=24, -3.34 at A=48, -1.28 at A=96), so the age tail is not where the return is lost.",
   "the guard changes the metric it targets: means of per-episode maxima fall 274.3 -> 133.3-179.1 (global worst 370 -> 186-324 across guarded arms); coverage stays 1.00 with 0 never-investigated hosts, i.e. no coverage collapse. The mechanism acts; it does not pay in return. Unguarded lancer coverage was already 1.000, so the guard bought freshness, not coverage.",
   "A is not a maximum and cannot be: observed overshoot is 62.8-119.1 ticks above threshold (one pending action per agent, 2-tick Analyse latency, illegal-to-analyse hosts and 42-198 urgent-rule deferrals per episode).",
   "maxage48 is statistically indistinguishable from the strict coverage guard (-0.22 CI[-6.78,+6.53]), so there is no reason to prefer the more complex mechanism.",
   "the tested privileged scorer improves unguarded return (+16.22 CI[+6.66,+25.56]) but is not an upper bound on ordering choices: it is a greedy per-host onset-likelihood scorer that ignores action cost and timing, and its own age metrics are worse (mean-of-maxima 371.0 vs unguarded lancer 274.3). Its coverage 0.284 is a mean 54.97 never-investigated hosts of a seed-dependent 57-96 (mean 76.3) defendable universe, an association with the return gain, not a demonstrated cause. Under coverage guards its edge over lancer vanishes (strict -3.12 CI[-12.16,+6.00], maxage48 -1.97 CI[-12.09,+7.22]); those upper bounds do not exclude a +5 effect."
  ]
 },
